{title: Let Him Go Up}
{subtitle: 2 Chronicles 36:21–23}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 83}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] |
| [Dm] | [Bb] | ×4

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]The land lay desolate in [Bb]si[Dm]lence
Seventy years of sabbath [Bb]kept
[Dm]The word of Jeremiah ful[Bb]filled
[C]The desert days were not [Bb]forgotten
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Dm]The God of heaven gave the [Bb]earth
[C]He appointed me to build [Dm]a house
In Jerusalem which is in Ju[Bb]dah
May the [C]Lord his God be with him
Let him go up
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Dm] | [Bb] | [Dm] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm]In the first year of his [Bb]reign
[Dm]Cyrus king of Persia [Bb]spoke
[Dm]He stirred the spirit of the [Bb]king
A [C]proclamation went throughout the [Bb]land
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Dm] | [Bb] | [Dm] | [Bb] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
So that the word might be accom[C]plished
The Lord stirred up the spir[Dm]it
[Bb]And he put it in writ[C]ing
Across the kingdoms of the [Dm]earth
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The God of heaven gave the [Bb]earth
He [C]appointed me to build a [Dm]house
In Jerusalem which is in Ju[Bb]dah
May the [C]Lord his God be with him
Let him go up
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [Dm] | [Bb] | [Dm] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Dm]Any of you who are of his peo[Bb]ple
